{"type":"data","nodes":[null,{"type":"data","data":[{"tree":1},[2,20],{"slug":3,"title":4,"pages":5},"start","Start",[6,14],{"siteId":7,"section":3,"slug":8,"path":9,"title":10,"description":11,"order":12,"verified":13},"watch","install","/content/watch/docs/start/install.md","Install","Prebuilt binaries, the Docker image, building from Zig source, or installing through NullHub.",1,"v2026.5.29",{"siteId":7,"section":3,"slug":15,"path":16,"title":17,"description":18,"order":19,"verified":13},"quickstart","/content/watch/docs/start/quickstart.md","Quickstart","Seed demo data, start the API, and inspect your first runs in five minutes.",2,{"slug":21,"title":22,"pages":23},"reference","Reference",[24,29],{"siteId":7,"section":21,"slug":25,"path":26,"title":27,"description":28,"order":12,"verified":13},"api","/content/watch/docs/reference/api.md","HTTP API","Endpoints, data model, query parameters and token auth for the NullWatch JSON API.",{"siteId":7,"section":21,"slug":30,"path":31,"title":32,"description":33,"order":19,"verified":13},"cli","/content/watch/docs/reference/cli.md","CLI","Every NullWatch command — serve, query, ingest, demo-seed — with flags and examples."],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"doc":1,"raw":10,"dateModified":31,"sectionTitle":32,"prev":33,"next":39},{"siteId":2,"section":3,"slug":4,"path":5,"title":6,"description":7,"order":8,"verified":9,"body":10,"html":11,"toc":12},"watch","start","quickstart","/content/watch/docs/start/quickstart.md","Quickstart","Seed demo data, start the API, and inspect your first runs in five minutes.",2,"v2026.5.29","\nThe fastest way to understand NullWatch is to let it cook with its own ingredients: `demo-seed` creates a complete local dataset — runs, spans, evals, costs, failures — with no API keys, no hosted services and no running agent.\n\n## 1. Seed the demo dataset\n\n```bash\nzig build run -- demo-seed\n```\n\nThis is deterministic and idempotent: run it twice and you get the same three scenarios, not six. It seeds:\n\n- a passing code-review run,\n- a failed tool-call run,\n- a handoff/retry run with checkpoint context.\n\n## 2. Query from the CLI\n\nYou don't need the server running to read local data:\n\n```bash\nzig build run -- runs --limit 20\nzig build run -- run demo-tool-failure\nzig build run -- summary\n```\n\n`run \u003Crun-id>` shows a single run in detail — its spans, evals and computed summary. `summary` aggregates across everything stored.\n\n## 3. Start the API and read it over HTTP\n\n```bash\nzig build run -- serve\n```\n\nThe server listens on `127.0.0.1:7710` by default. In another terminal:\n\n```bash\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:7710/health\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:7710/v1/runs?limit=20\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:7710/v1/runs/demo-tool-failure\n```\n\nEvery endpoint returns JSON. The full surface is in the [API reference](/docs/reference/api/).\n\n## 4. Ingest something yourself\n\nSpans and evals can be written from the CLI or over HTTP. From the CLI:\n\n```bash\nzig build run -- ingest-eval --json '{\n  \"run_id\": \"run-123\",\n  \"eval_key\": \"helpfulness\",\n  \"scorer\": \"llm-judge\",\n  \"score\": 0.94,\n  \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n  \"dataset\": \"prod-shadow\"\n}'\n```\n\nOver HTTP:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:7710/v1/spans \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\n    \"run_id\": \"run-123\",\n    \"trace_id\": \"trace-123\",\n    \"span_id\": \"span-1\",\n    \"source\": \"nullclaw\",\n    \"operation\": \"tool.call\",\n    \"status\": \"ok\",\n    \"started_at_ms\": 1710000000000,\n    \"ended_at_ms\": 1710000000140,\n    \"tool_name\": \"bash\"\n  }'\n```\n\n## 5. Point NullClaw at it\n\nNullWatch speaks OTLP/HTTP JSON on `/v1/traces` and `/otlp/v1/traces`, so it works as a small local OpenTelemetry trace sink. Point [NullClaw](https://claw.nullmenu.ai/)'s diagnostics OTLP endpoint at `http://127.0.0.1:7710` and its spans map into NullWatch runs — a `nullwatch.run_id` attribute on a span groups it under that run.\n\n## 6. Render it in NullHub\n\nFor the flight-recorder view, seed and serve:\n\n```bash\nzig build run -- demo-seed\nzig build run -- serve --port 7710\n```\n\nThen start [NullHub](https://hub.nullmenu.ai/) with `NULLWATCH_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7710` and open its Observability page. You'll see the seeded runs with token usage, cost and failure context — NullWatch stores and computes, NullHub draws.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Everything so far touched only local files under `~/.nullwatch/data`. Nothing was sent anywhere.\n\nNext: the full [CLI reference](/docs/reference/cli/) and [API reference](/docs/reference/api/).\n","\u003Cp>The fastest way to understand NullWatch is to let it cook with its own ingredients: \u003Ccode>demo-seed\u003C/code> creates a complete local dataset — runs, spans, evals, costs, failures — with no API keys, no hosted services and no running agent.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"1-seed-the-demo-dataset\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-label-1-seed-the-demo-dataset\">\u003Cspan id=\"heading-label-1-seed-the-demo-dataset\">1. Seed the demo dataset\u003C/span>\u003Ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#1-seed-the-demo-dataset\" aria-label=\"Permalink to 1. Seed the demo dataset\" data-pagefind-ignore>\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\">#\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cfigure class=\"code-figure\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Cpre class=\"shiki null-kitchen\" style=\"background-color:#0a0806;color:#d9d1c3\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> demo-seed\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cbutton class=\"code-copy\" type=\"button\" data-code data-pagefind-ignore aria-live=\"polite\">copy\u003C/button>\u003C/figure>\n\u003Cp>This is deterministic and idempotent: run it twice and you get the same three scenarios, not six. It seeds:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>a passing code-review run,\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>a failed tool-call run,\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>a handoff/retry run with checkpoint context.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"2-query-from-the-cli\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-label-2-query-from-the-cli\">\u003Cspan id=\"heading-label-2-query-from-the-cli\">2. Query from the CLI\u003C/span>\u003Ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#2-query-from-the-cli\" aria-label=\"Permalink to 2. Query from the CLI\" data-pagefind-ignore>\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\">#\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>You don&#39;t need the server running to read local data:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cfigure class=\"code-figure\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Cpre class=\"shiki null-kitchen\" style=\"background-color:#0a0806;color:#d9d1c3\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> runs\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --limit\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#D9A441\"> 20\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> demo-tool-failure\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> summary\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cbutton class=\"code-copy\" type=\"button\" data-code data-pagefind-ignore aria-live=\"polite\">copy\u003C/button>\u003C/figure>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>run &lt;run-id&gt;\u003C/code> shows a single run in detail — its spans, evals and computed summary. \u003Ccode>summary\u003C/code> aggregates across everything stored.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"3-start-the-api-and-read-it-over-http\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-label-3-start-the-api-and-read-it-over-http\">\u003Cspan id=\"heading-label-3-start-the-api-and-read-it-over-http\">3. Start the API and read it over HTTP\u003C/span>\u003Ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#3-start-the-api-and-read-it-over-http\" aria-label=\"Permalink to 3. Start the API and read it over HTTP\" data-pagefind-ignore>\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\">#\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cfigure class=\"code-figure\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Cpre class=\"shiki null-kitchen\" style=\"background-color:#0a0806;color:#d9d1c3\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> serve\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cbutton class=\"code-copy\" type=\"button\" data-code data-pagefind-ignore aria-live=\"polite\">copy\u003C/button>\u003C/figure>\n\u003Cp>The server listens on \u003Ccode>127.0.0.1:7710\u003C/code> by default. In another terminal:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cfigure class=\"code-figure\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Cpre class=\"shiki null-kitchen\" style=\"background-color:#0a0806;color:#d9d1c3\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">curl\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> http://127.0.0.1:7710/health\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">curl\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> http://127.0.0.1:7710/v1/runs?limit=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#D9A441\">20\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">curl\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> http://127.0.0.1:7710/v1/runs/demo-tool-failure\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cbutton class=\"code-copy\" type=\"button\" data-code data-pagefind-ignore aria-live=\"polite\">copy\u003C/button>\u003C/figure>\n\u003Cp>Every endpoint returns JSON. The full surface is in the \u003Ca href=\"/docs/reference/api/\">API reference\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"4-ingest-something-yourself\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-label-4-ingest-something-yourself\">\u003Cspan id=\"heading-label-4-ingest-something-yourself\">4. Ingest something yourself\u003C/span>\u003Ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#4-ingest-something-yourself\" aria-label=\"Permalink to 4. Ingest something yourself\" data-pagefind-ignore>\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\">#\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>Spans and evals can be written from the CLI or over HTTP. From the CLI:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cfigure class=\"code-figure\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Cpre class=\"shiki null-kitchen\" style=\"background-color:#0a0806;color:#d9d1c3\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> ingest-eval\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --json\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> '{\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"run_id\": \"run-123\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"eval_key\": \"helpfulness\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"scorer\": \"llm-judge\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"score\": 0.94,\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"verdict\": \"pass\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  \"dataset\": \"prod-shadow\"\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">}'\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cbutton class=\"code-copy\" type=\"button\" data-code data-pagefind-ignore aria-live=\"polite\">copy\u003C/button>\u003C/figure>\n\u003Cp>Over HTTP:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cfigure class=\"code-figure\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Cpre class=\"shiki null-kitchen\" style=\"background-color:#0a0806;color:#d9d1c3\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">curl\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> -X\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> POST\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> http://127.0.0.1:7710/v1/spans\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#D9A441\"> \\\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  -H\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> 'content-type: application/json'\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#D9A441\"> \\\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  -d\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> '{\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">    \"run_id\": \"run-123\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">    \"trace_id\": \"trace-123\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">    \"span_id\": \"span-1\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">    \"source\": \"nullclaw\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">    \"operation\": \"tool.call\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">    \"status\": \"ok\",\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">    \"started_at_ms\": 1710000000000,\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">    \"ended_at_ms\": 1710000000140,\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">    \"tool_name\": \"bash\"\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\">  }'\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cbutton class=\"code-copy\" type=\"button\" data-code data-pagefind-ignore aria-live=\"polite\">copy\u003C/button>\u003C/figure>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"5-point-nullclaw-at-it\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-label-5-point-nullclaw-at-it\">\u003Cspan id=\"heading-label-5-point-nullclaw-at-it\">5. Point NullClaw at it\u003C/span>\u003Ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#5-point-nullclaw-at-it\" aria-label=\"Permalink to 5. Point NullClaw at it\" data-pagefind-ignore>\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\">#\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>NullWatch speaks OTLP/HTTP JSON on \u003Ccode>/v1/traces\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode>/otlp/v1/traces\u003C/code>, so it works as a small local OpenTelemetry trace sink. Point \u003Ca href=\"https://claw.nullmenu.ai/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" aria-label=\"NullClaw (opens in a new tab)\">NullClaw\u003Csvg class=\"functional-icon external-icon\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\">\u003Cg stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.75\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\u003Cpath d=\"M8 16 16 8\">\u003C/path>\u003Cpath d=\"M10 8h6v6\">\u003C/path>\u003C/g>\u003C/svg>\u003C/a>&#39;s diagnostics OTLP endpoint at \u003Ccode>http://127.0.0.1:7710\u003C/code> and its spans map into NullWatch runs — a \u003Ccode>nullwatch.run_id\u003C/code> attribute on a span groups it under that run.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"6-render-it-in-nullhub\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-label-6-render-it-in-nullhub\">\u003Cspan id=\"heading-label-6-render-it-in-nullhub\">6. Render it in NullHub\u003C/span>\u003Ca class=\"heading-anchor\" href=\"#6-render-it-in-nullhub\" aria-label=\"Permalink to 6. Render it in NullHub\" data-pagefind-ignore>\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\">#\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>For the flight-recorder view, seed and serve:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cfigure class=\"code-figure\" data-lang=\"bash\">\u003Cpre class=\"shiki null-kitchen\" style=\"background-color:#0a0806;color:#d9d1c3\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> demo-seed\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:#ECE5D8\">zig\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> run\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> serve\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#C9B795\"> --port\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:#D9A441\"> 7710\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cbutton class=\"code-copy\" type=\"button\" data-code data-pagefind-ignore aria-live=\"polite\">copy\u003C/button>\u003C/figure>\n\u003Cp>Then start \u003Ca href=\"https://hub.nullmenu.ai/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" aria-label=\"NullHub (opens in a new tab)\">NullHub\u003Csvg class=\"functional-icon external-icon\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\">\u003Cg stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.75\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\u003Cpath d=\"M8 16 16 8\">\u003C/path>\u003Cpath d=\"M10 8h6v6\">\u003C/path>\u003C/g>\u003C/svg>\u003C/a> with \u003Ccode>NULLWATCH_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7710\u003C/code> and open its Observability page. You&#39;ll see the seeded runs with token usage, cost and failure context — NullWatch stores and computes, NullHub draws.\u003C/p>\n\u003Caside class=\"callout callout--tip\">\u003Cdiv class=\"callout-title\">Tip\u003C/div>\u003Cp>Everything so far touched only local files under \u003Ccode>~/.nullwatch/data\u003C/code>. Nothing was sent anywhere.\u003C/p>\n\u003C/aside>\n\u003Cp>Next: the full \u003Ca href=\"/docs/reference/cli/\">CLI reference\u003C/a> and \u003Ca href=\"/docs/reference/api/\">API reference\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\n",[13,16,19,22,25,28],{"id":14,"text":15,"depth":8},"1-seed-the-demo-dataset","1. Seed the demo dataset",{"id":17,"text":18,"depth":8},"2-query-from-the-cli","2. Query from the CLI",{"id":20,"text":21,"depth":8},"3-start-the-api-and-read-it-over-http","3. Start the API and read it over HTTP",{"id":23,"text":24,"depth":8},"4-ingest-something-yourself","4. Ingest something yourself",{"id":26,"text":27,"depth":8},"5-point-nullclaw-at-it","5. Point NullClaw at it",{"id":29,"text":30,"depth":8},"6-render-it-in-nullhub","6. Render it in NullHub","2026-07-16","Start",{"siteId":2,"section":3,"slug":34,"path":35,"title":36,"description":37,"order":38,"verified":9,"sectionTitle":32},"install","/content/watch/docs/start/install.md","Install","Prebuilt binaries, the Docker image, building from Zig source, or installing through NullHub.",1,{"siteId":2,"section":40,"slug":41,"path":42,"title":43,"description":44,"order":38,"verified":9,"sectionTitle":45},"reference","api","/content/watch/docs/reference/api.md","HTTP API","Endpoints, data model, query parameters and token auth for the NullWatch JSON API.","Reference"],"uses":{"params":["section","slug"]}}]}
